config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_TERMINAL
	bool "cadr-terminal"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	help
	  The screen: the program on the processing system that shows the
	  CADR's display to a VNC viewer.  The display board keeps no
	  frame buffer in the fabric --- the picture is written into the
	  display's own region of DDR --- so this maps that region and
	  serves it over RFB, and needs no new fabric at all.

	  READ-ONLY: no keyboard, no mouse, no pointer.  Those are the
	  I/O board's and the I/O board is not in the fabric; a viewer's
	  input is read, counted and dropped.

	  It has an init script, as cadr-disk-pack does and unlike
	  cadr-console: a viewer connects when somebody wants to look, and
	  nothing is on the bus while nobody does.
